# Google Cloud safety

## Read-only default

List/describe/get are fine when GCP work is authorized. Do **not**:

- delete projects, VMs, disks, clusters, buckets, or objects
- grant broad IAM (`roles/owner`, `allUsers`, org-wide bindings)
- create or download service-account keys
- disable billing or wipe firewall rules

…unless the user gave an explicit verb this turn naming the resource.

## Irreversible

Project deletes, production cluster deletes, and public bucket ACL changes:
state the risk in one sentence and only proceed when clearly authorized
(`global-execute-first` scope grill for irreversible loss).

## Secrets

Never paste SA keys, refresh tokens, or application-default credentials
into chat or commits — prefer `vault`.
